As a PAM Engineer

I want to research and define a Limited Auditor access model in CyberArk, including how session recording and non-session recording access is granted or restricted

So that we can provide advanced end users with appropriate visibility into CyberArk activity without granting full PAM Engineer capabilities

Notes: 

Session Recording Access

View session recordings (PSM / SWS) for:

Assigned platforms (e.g., Linux, Windows, App-specific)

Authorized safes tied to recording storage

View session metadata:

User activity

Connection timestamps

Ability to search and review recordings for audit / troubleshooting purposes

Access controlled via:

Safe-level permissions for recording safes

AD group membership aligned to platform or team scope

Non-Session Recording (Audit Visibility)
View audit logs and activity records

Review privileged account usage history

Access compliance and reporting data

Search user and account activity across the environment

Leverages:

Built-in Global Auditor (or equivalent) role for read-only audit visibility

AC1: Document process in confluence 

AC2: Review with PAM Team

AC3: Work with PO/SM to create stories for future work
